        <mxCell id="c50" value="&lt;i&gt;64 employees recorded 20,030 hours of manufacturing overtime by work date. The curve stays within 1.6 points of the diagonal: the five largest totals hold 8.4% (an even spread would give 7.8%) and the ten largest 16.6% (15.6%). A concentrated pattern would rise steeply and pass one half within a handful of names.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="488" width="860" height="42" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
